  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya Food Crisis &amp; Drought 2021-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is a worsening food and nutrition situation in Kenya, attributed mainly to the poor performance of the OND 2020 and the MAM 2021
Projected 1,913,265 persons will need assistance (34% increase from the 1.4 million February 2021)
At least 12 Counties affected -&#xa0;Marsabit, Mandera, Garissa, Wajir, Kilifi, Tana River, Lamu, Samburu, Kitui, Lamu, Isiolo and Laikipia are in the alert drought phase
The worst affected counties-&#xa0; Turkana, Garissa, Wajir and Marsabit counties which have about 5% of their populations in IPC 4 (NDMA, July 2021).
&#xa0;
British Red Cross General funds support to the KRCS&#x2019; 2021 Drought appeal in Samburu and Makueni Counties. multi-purpose cash support targets 1,050 households</narrative>
  </description>
